    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Show that the diagonal of a square of side length $a$ is $a\\sqrt{2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$d=\\sqrt{a^2+a^2}=\\sqrt{2a^2}=a\\sqrt{2}$.",
      "worked": "The diagonal divides the square into two right-angled triangles, each with perpendicular sides of length $a$. Let the diagonal have length $d$. By Pythagoras’ theorem:\n$$\\begin{align*}d^2&=a^2+a^2\\\\d^2&=2a^2\\\\d&=\\sqrt{2a^2}\\\\d&=a\\sqrt{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a$ is a side length, $a>0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
